sentences.text:
The appellants are ordered to be released on bail in connection with F.I.R. registered as C.R. No. 11199038250394/2025 registered with Nabipur Police Station, District Bharuch, on executing a bond of Rs.1,00,000/- (Rupees One Lakh only) with one surety of NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.A/2575/2025 ORDER DATED: 01/04/2026 undefined the like amount qua appellant of Cr.M.A.2576/2025 and on executing a bond of Rs.25,000/- (Rupees Twenty Five Thousand only) each with one surety of the like amount each qua other appellant, to the satisfaction of the trial Court and subject to the conditions that they shall; [a] not take undue advantage of liberty or misuse liberty; [b] not act in a manner injurious to the interest of the prosecution;
[c] surrender passport, if any, to the lower court within a week;
[d] not leave the State of Gujarat without prior permission of the Sessions Court concerned;
[e] furnish the present address of residence to the I.O. and also to the Court at the time of execution of the bond and shall not change the residence without prior intimation to the I.O.;
[f] all the appellants to file an undertaking that the appellants will reconstruct the demolished portion of the house in question within a period of two months or thereabouts from the date of their release in the same position as it was prior to the demolition, before the NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.A/2575/2025 ORDER DATED: 01/04/2026 undefined learned Trial Court within a period of Salim Ahmedshah Diwan vs State Of Gujarat on 1 April, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/160918913/
3 two days from the date of their release and before this Court within a period of one week from the date of their release; [g] appellant of Cr.M.A. 2576/2025 to mark presence once a week for a period of three months, thereafter, once a fortnight for a period of three months and thereafter, once a months for a period of six months before the concerned police station.
[h] other appellants to mark presence once a month for a period of one year before the concerned police station.
9. The Authorities will release the appellants only if they are not required in connection with any other offence for the time being.

